Cinematic Site Components — references/motion-patterns.md
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The motion pattern library re-implements the thirty demo pages of Cinematic
Site Components: the sixteen that need no library, and the fourteen built on
GSAP and ScrollTrigger, which are rewritten here in CSS (scroll-driven
animations, scroll-snap, sticky positioning, clip-path and masks) and the
Web Animations API so that nothing is loaded.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/robonuggets/cinematic-site-components
  Author:    Jay from RoboLabs
  License:   MIT
  Changes:   Derived, not copied. Every pattern rewritten under an lm-*
             namespace, reading the host template's design tokens instead
             of a hard-coded palette; the global reset, the generic class
             names and the fixed attribution bar dropped; ARIA, keyboard
             paths, reduced-motion handling, print handling and a
             fail-visible fallback for IntersectionObserver added; every
             GSAP dependency replaced, since GSAP could not be bundled.

